goal: Deliver one real provenance-bound Qwen3-0.6B six-member SLM2 composition through the production Companion source operation, independent structural inspection, scalar/native/browser numerical proof, useful-model qualification, P2P-or-convert acquisition, genuine clean-profile multi-turn chat, both MemoryEndpoints lanes, source-controlled release, deployment, and HTTPS readback.

start:
  - Read workspace.uai, .uai/totem.uai, .uai/taboo.uai, the canonical memory, the report decision index, and the current Companion memory.
  - Verify root, branch, clean/known worktree state, remote equality, protected trees, frozen source/profile identities, and current test baseline.
  - Preserve every immutable historical operation, especially /10; create wholly new preregistered identities for real execution.

immediate_work:
  - Complete this bounded UAI consolidation and commit/push it green.
  - Implement the exclusive restart-safe production source owner with bounded pinned-source streaming, contained converter process custody, cancellation, immutable terminal evidence, and independent six-member inspection.
  - Keep listener operation-not-available until the real owner exists; never wire a queued fiction or fixture executor.
  - Load the sole browser client and delete the old bridge and one-file acquisition semantics only after matching production operation/transfer contracts are green.

ordered_gates:
  - Contract and hostile vectors.
  - Wholly new output-free registration and one-shot source operation.
  - Six-member semantic inspection.
  - Pinned source to scalar-native first divergence.
  - Optimized-native and real-browser-WASM parity.
  - Sealed source/quantized/browser behavioral qualification.
  - Exact peer import or explicit local conversion in product UI.
  - Fresh-profile multi-turn chat, exactly-once render, cancellation, privacy, and profile deletion.
  - Direct MemoryEndpoints agent coordination receipts and separate TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin login/continuity/cleanup receipts.
  - Package/site release, publication logs, synchronized documentation, deployment, rollback, and HTTPS readback.

hard_rules:
  - No legacy, compatibility, migration, alias, fallback, repair, hidden retry, best-of-N, debt, test weakening, fabricated evidence, or counter inflation.
  - Keep model/raw evidence/credentials outside Git and private prompts out of public records.
  - Duplicate prelaunch memory only when every maintained copy stays current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  - Commit and push each coherent green major change; deploy each affected site whenever its complete gate passes.
